// Follows: what is told answered by what follows from it and how it feels, read off the graph
// (src/research/conceptnet.ts, src/research/feeling.ts). Written by scripts/pack.mjs from
// sources/follows (edit those, not this).
Requires(Core(), Basic())

// How a word feels, from -4 (worst) to 4 (best): learned from the VADER lexicon the first time
// a message says the word, kept on the written word (`Word_broken Valence(-2.1)`).
Concept(Valence(), IsA(Relation()))

// What an event leads to, as ConceptNet says it: what it causes, makes one want, has happen in
// it, takes first, is done for. Looked up when a message tells of the event.
Concept(CausesDesire(), IsA(Relation()))

Concept(HasSubevent(), IsA(Relation()))

Concept(HasFirstSubevent(), IsA(Relation()))

Concept(HasLastSubevent(), IsA(Relation()))

Concept(HasPrerequisite(), IsA(Relation()))

Concept(MotivatedByGoal(), IsA(Relation()))

Concept(Entails(), IsA(Relation()))

// What follows from what was told, and how it felt: a reply's matter.
Concept(Follows(), IsA(Result()))

// Where the lexicon and the common sense come from, and under what license.
Concept(Vader(), IsA(LearningSource()), License("MIT"))

Concept(ConceptNet(), IsA(LearningSource()), License("CC BY-SA 4.0"))

// Talk that keeps company rather than asks: a greeting, and how one is doing. When something bad
// was told before, small talk asks after it (`CheckIn`), once.
Concept(SmallTalk(), IsA(Category()))

Concept(Greeting(), IsA(SmallTalk()))

Concept(DoingWell(), IsA(SmallTalk()))

// Something going on in the life of the one talking, as they told it ("your mom is sick"), kept
// on Me with how bad it felt; and that it was asked after.
Concept(Concern(), IsA(Relation()))

Concept(CheckedIn(), IsA(Relation()))

Concept(CheckIn(), IsA(Result()))

// What a reply offered ("Do you want to talk about it?"): kept on Self with the words it was said in,
// so a yes or no next answers it (`OfferAnswered`).
Concept(Offered(), IsA(Relation()))

Concept(OfferAnswered(), IsA(Result()))

Concept(TalkingItOver(), IsA(Data()))
